# threshold-ledger — the mesh's scattered inline magic numbers as ONE data file
# (uxn-threshold-ledger, gates-as-data stage 2, 2026-07-23). Each row is a calibrated
# predicate: params are the RUNTIME inputs, consts are the CALIBRATED numbers (k=v pairs,
# naturals only), the template is the s-expr the pinned evaluator runs. Recalibration is a
# diff on the consts column of THIS file, never a script edit; consumers resolve their
# defaults through `mesh-sexpr-gate --const <gate> <k>` (env > ledger > inline fallback),
# and mesh-rom-calibrate --ledger drives every row through ./threshold-fixtures against a
# native-shell twin (DIVERGE = expression/evaluator drift; 16-bit overflow = DOMAIN).
#
# evaluator-sha1: b3c917e97894502018735e15d3448aee92b59ffb   (lisp-eval.rom)
#
# format: name | params (runtime inputs, bound positionally) | consts k=v… | template
# clear-fresh:  1 FRESH · 0 STALE — mesh-clear's handoff budget (was MESH_CLEAR_FRESH_SECS 900 inline)
# load-gate:    0 SKIP-quiet · 1 PROCEED · 2 SKIP-load — l1c is centi-load1 (load1*100),
#               thr = nproc*k centi = nproc*0.90 (was DEFAULT_THR awk n*0.9); quiet [q0,q1) end-exclusive
# lease-margin: 1 OK · 0 RED — lease >= k*cadence (the documented cadence*2 convention)
clear-fresh  | age            | fresh=900      | (if (<= age fresh) 1 0)
load-gate    | l1c hour nproc | k=90 q0=1 q1=6 | (if (if (>= hour q0) (< hour q1) 0) 0 (if (> l1c (* k nproc)) 2 1))
lease-margin | cad lease      | k=2            | (if (>= lease (* k cad)) 1 0)
